Cable 's inclusion in the potential sequel was confirmed by the character Deadpool , breaking the fourth wall , in the post-credit scene of the first film . Domino , a character with connections to Cable in the comics , was also believed to be featured in the sequel . By the first film 's release , 20th Century Fox had green - lit a sequel , with writers Rhett Reese and Paul Wernick returning to write the screenplay . Though director Tim Miller and producer / star Ryan Reynolds were not confirmed for the sequel at the time , Fox was `` intent on keeping the creative team together '' . Miller and Reynolds ' involvement was confirmed at the 2016 CinemaCon that April , though Miller had still not formally signed on to direct the sequel yet . He began work developing the script with the writers , while Reynolds had signed a new contract granting him `` casting approval and other creative controls '' . It has to tonally and stylistically be as fresh and original ( as the first film ) . That 's a big challenge especially because they had 10 years to gestate on the first movie and we do n't have that kind of time on the second movie .","entities":["Rhett Reese","Paul Wernick","Deadpool","Domino","Ryan Reynolds","2016 CinemaCon","screenplay","Tim Miller","first film","Cable","20th Century Fox","Deadpool 2"],"facts":["'Deadpool' Scribes Rhett Reese & Paul Wernick On This Awards Season's Biggest Surprise Candidate -RELATED_TO-> Paul Wernick","Deadpool -RELATED_TO-> Eddie Murphy","Rhett Reese -CREATED-> That's a wrap! Deadpool 2 is in the can!","'Deadpool' Scribes Rhett Reese & Paul Wernick On This Awards Season's Biggest Surprise Candidate -RELATED_TO-> Rhett Reese","Deadpool -RELATED_TO-> X-Force"]}
