It was organised by the British Museum and the Prince of Wales Museum in partnership with Sir Dorabji Tata Trust , Sir Ratan Tata Trust and Navajbai Ratan Tata Trust , all set up by luminaries from the Parsi community , who are descendants of Persian Zoroastrians , who hold Cyrus in great regard , as many scholars consider him as a follower of Zoroastrianism . Freedom Sculpture ( edit ) Main article : Freedom Sculpture The freedom sculpture The Freedom Sculpture ( Persian : تندیس آزادی ‎ ) is a gold and silver statue located on Santa Monica Boulevard in the Beverly Hills , California . The design of the Freedom Sculpture was created by artist and architect Cecil Balmond . It is themed on the Cyrus Cylinder from 2,500 years ago , which is sometimes considered the first declaration of human rights . It commemorates the declaration of Cyrus the Great , King of ancient Iran , granting individual and religious freedoms to those within his empire . See also ( edit ) Behistun inscriptions Persepolis Fortification Archive Cyrus 's edict Notes ( edit ) ^ Jump up to : `` The Cyrus Cylinder ( British Museum database ) '' .","entities":["Cyrus Cylinder","California","human rights","Prince of Wales Museum","Sir Dorabji Tata Trust","Sir Ratan Tata Trust","Navajbai Ratan Tata Trust","Parsi community","Persian Zoroastrians","Cyrus the Great","Zoroastrianism","Freedom Sculpture","Santa Monica Boulevard","Beverly Hills","Cecil Balmond"],"facts":["Cyrus Cylinder -RELATED_TO-> Achaemenid Empire","Cyrus Cylinder -RELATED_TO-> Babylon","Cyrus Cylinder -RELATED_TO-> Cyrus","Cyrus Cylinder -RELATED_TO-> universal human rights","Cyrus Cylinder -RELATED_TO-> Akkadian cuneiform script"]}

