The song appears on the soundtrack of the 2014 film Inherent Vice , directed by Paul Thomas Anderson . The song appears twice in the 2008 documentary film Japan : A Story of Love and Hate , directed by Sean McAllister . The song appears in episode 2 of The Man in the High Castle , in a world where the American west coast is occupied by Imperial Japan . Legacy ( edit ) An instrumental version of the song was played by NASA over the radio for the Gemini VII astronauts as mood music and became one of the first pieces of music sent to humans in space On March 16 , 1999 , Japan Post issued a stamp that commemorated the song . The stamp is listed in the Scott Standard Postage Stamp Catalogue as Japan number 2666 with a face value of 50 yen . Sakamoto died on August 12 , 1985 , in the crash of Japan Airlines Flight 123 , the deadliest single - aircraft accident in history . References ( edit ) Jump up ^ `` A Brief History of `` I Look Up as I Walk '' in Anime atelier emily `` . Formeinfullbloom.wordpress.com.","entities":["Sakamoto","Inherent Vice","Paul Thomas Anderson","Japan: A Story of Love and Hate","Sean McAllister","The Man in the High Castle","American west coast","Imperial Japan","instrumental version of Sukiyaki","NASA","Gemini VII astronauts","stamp commemorating Sukiyaki","Scott Standard Postage Stamp Catalogue","crash of Japan Airlines Flight 123","Japan Airlines"],"facts":["Sukiyaki -RELATED_TO-> Anoko No Namaewa Nantenkana","Sukiyaki -RELATED_TO-> Toshiba-EMI","Sakamoto -PARTICIPATED_IN-> Japan Airlines Flight 123 crash","わたし の 愛 唱歌 シリーズ 第 9 集 郵便 切手 -RELATED_TO-> Japan Post","Sukiyaki -RELATED_TO-> Capitol / EMI Records"]}
