Those two championships mark the Eagles as the only NFL team ever to win back - to - back championships by shutouts , defeating the Chicago Cardinals , 7 -- 0 , in 1948 -- in a blizzard -- and the Los Angeles Rams , 14 -- 0 , in 1949 . After the 1957 season , the Eagles moved from Connie Mack Stadium to Franklin Field at the University of Pennsylvania . Franklin Field would seat over 60,000 for the Eagles , whereas Connie Mack had a capacity of 39,000 . The stadium switched from grass to AstroTurf in 1969 . It was the first NFL stadium to use artificial turf . In 1960 , the Eagles won their third NFL championship , under the leadership of future Pro Football Hall of Famers Norm Van Brocklin and Chuck Bednarik ; the head coach was Buck Shaw . The 1960 Eagles , by a score of 17 -- 13 , became the only team to defeat Vince Lombardi and his Green Bay Packers in the playoffs .","entities":["Pro Football Hall of Fame","NFL","Chicago Cardinals","Los Angeles Rams","Franklin Field","AstroTurf","Norm Van Brocklin","Chuck Bednarik","Buck Shaw","Vince Lombardi","Green Bay Packers","1948 NFL championship","1949 NFL championship","1960 NFL championship","1960 playoff game"],"facts":["Pro Football Hall of Fame -RELATED_TO-> Eagles Honor Roll","Greasy Neale -RELATED_TO-> Pro Football Hall of Fame","Bell -RELATED_TO-> Pro Football Hall of Fame","Bob Brown -RELATED_TO-> Pro Football Hall of Fame","Reggie White -RELATED_TO-> Pro Football Hall of Fame"]}
